<title>INDIA: India forex reserves drop to $23.81 bln on Dec 13.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves drop to $23.81 bln on Dec 13.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves fell to $23.81 billion on December 13, 1996 from $23.91 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Dec 13	Dec  6	 Dec 15</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,418	19,434	 17,344</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,347	 4,347	  4,429</p>
<p>    SDRs				    42	   125		5</p>
<p>    Total			     23,807	23,906	 21,778</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
